This evaluated data file is based on a software system built      5049 1451   24
around the nuclear model code TALYS [kon23], version 2.0. It is   5049 1451   25
part of a large collection of isotopic evaluations, all created by5049 1451   26
running the system with either adjusted or default input          5049 1451   27
parameters. This means that the data in the entire collection have5049 1451   28
been tested in detail for many isotopes against individual        5049 1451   29
experimental data, while for other isotopes it is only as good as 5049 1451   30
the global quality of TALYS at the moment. The mutual quality of  5049 1451   31
all individual data files is however consistent: The same set of  5049 1451   32
nuclear models is used and, equally important, the same ENDF-6    5049 1451   33
formatting procedures for each isotope. The data file has been    5049 1451   34
created automatically using the ENDF-6 format generator TEFAL.    5049 1451   35
                                                                  5049 1451   36
The resulting data file provides a complete representation of     5049 1451   37
nuclear data needed for transport, activation, damage, heating,   5049 1451   38
radioactivity, and shielding applications over the incident       5049 1451   39
neutron energy range from 1.e-11 to 200. MeV.                     5049 1451   40
                                                                  5049 1451   41
All transport and activation data for neutrons, charged particles,5049 1451   42
photons and residual nuclides are filed. This includes cross      5049 1451   43
sections, angular distributions, double-differential spectra,     5049 1451   44
isomeric production, discrete and continuum photon production     5049 1451   45
cross sections, residual production cross sections and recoils.   5049 1451   46
This general purpose evaluation can thus be used as both          5049 1451   47
transport and activation library.                                 5049 1451   48
                                                                  5049 1451   49
A complete set of covariance data is included, which is stored    5049 1451   50
in MF31-40.                                                       5049 1451   51
