***************************** T A L Y S **************************5049 1451   85
                                                                  5049 1451   86
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   5049 1451   87
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      5049 1451   88
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    5049 1451   89
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     5049 1451   90
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  5049 1451   91
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        5049 1451   92
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    5049 1451   93
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         5049 1451   94
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      5049 1451   95
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    5049 1451   96
stored in this data file:                                         5049 1451   97
                                                                  5049 1451   98
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   5049 1451   99
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     5049 1451  100
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 5049 1451  101
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   5049 1451  102
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                5049 1451  103
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   5049 1451  104
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    5049 1451  105
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        5049 1451  106
- Recoil data                                                     5049 1451  107
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           5049 1451  108
- Total particle energy spectra                                   5049 1451  109
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      5049 1451  110
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        5049 1451  111
- Residual production cross sections                              5049 1451  112
                                                                  5049 1451  113
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            5049 1451  114
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        5049 1451  115
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   5049 1451  116
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                5049 1451  117
