##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 5049 1451  311
                                                                  5049 1451  312
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  5049 1451  313
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     5049 1451  314
with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates TALYS runs using    5049 1451  315
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   5049 1451  316
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  5049 1451  317
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                5049 1451  318
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      5049 1451  319
   same reaction channel between different energies)              5049 1451  320
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      5049 1451  321
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               5049 1451  322
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      5049 1451  323
   different reaction channels for different energies)            5049 1451  324
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        5049 1451  325
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              5049 1451  326
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  5049 1451  327
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       5049 1451  328
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     5049 1451  329
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  5049 1451  330
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     5049 1451  331
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     5049 1451  332
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     5049 1451  333
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   5049 1451  334
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   5049 1451  335
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  5049 1451  336
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   5049 1451  337
                                                                  5049 1451  338
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  5049 1451  339
                                                                  5049 1451  340
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       5049 1451  341
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  5049 1451  342
are generated with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates       5049 1451  343
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   5049 1451  344
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         5049 1451  345
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  5049 1451  346
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      5049 1451  347
representation is used.                                           5049 1451  348
                                                                  5049 1451  349
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      5049 1451  350
                                                                  5049 1451  351
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  5049 1451  352
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             5049 1451  353
